    "created_at": "2017-06-21T18:45:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-21T18:45:04Z",
    "body": "So, we should definitely tighten up \"successfully obtained\". That either means \"not a network error\" or \"not a network error and is an OK status\". It sounds like https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/6211 indicates it's just \"network error\", i.e. we download 404s successfully?\r\n\r\nWe could indeed fire an error event, although I'm not sure what the web site would do with such data. Is Firefox interested in implementing that? Anyone else?\r\n\r\nTagging in @cdumez, maybe @jeisinger?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
